119:**Send states.** `pending → sending → sent | failed(reason)`. A delivery takes a two-minute lease before calling the provider, and the call times out after 30 seconds. A clear rejection (`E_RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` and other coded errors) returns the send to `pending` and the message is retried after 30 s, 60 s, and 120 s; the fourth rejection fails it. Permanent rejections (`E_RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED`, sender and header errors) fail at once. An error without a code, a timeout, or a lease that expired with no outcome fails the send as `unknown`, and it is never resent automatically. A message the queue dead-letters fails its send too (`abandoned`, or `rejected` after earlier rejections).
